- **Key Feature**: The difference arises solely from the presence of different numbers of isotopes of one or more element.
- **Example**:
  - In a molecule of water (H₂O), isotopomers would include:
    - H₂O (all hydrogen atoms are ¹H)
    - D₂O (all hydrogen atoms are ²H or deuterium)
