1. Temperature-Responsive Polymers:

The most well-known temperature-responsive polymer is poly-poly-lactin (PL-12-1-3), which exhibits a sharp transition in temperature. The transition temperature can be tuned by changing the polymer's structure or introducing other components.

a) Poly-12-1-3 (PL-12-1-3) and its variants: These polymers have a lower lower transition temperature (LCST) around around 35°C. The LCST is the temperature at which the polymer transitions from a low-water-soluble state to a swollen, high-water-soluble state.

