   \[
   \binom{12}{11} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{11} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{1} = \binom{12}{11} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 12 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = \frac{12}{4096}
   \]

4. **Probability of exactly 12 heads**:  
   \[
   \binom{12}{12} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{0} = \binom{12}{12} \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = 1 \left(\frac{1}{2}\right)^{12} = \frac{1}{4096}
   \]

The probability of getting at least 9 heads is the sum of these probabilities:  
\[
\frac{55}{4096} + \frac{66}{4096} + \frac{12}{4096} + \frac{1}{4096} = \frac{55 + 66 + 12 + 1}{4096} = \frac{134}{4096} = \frac{67}{2048}
