   \]  
   Thus, \( \mu_n(C) \leq \mu(C) + \epsilon \).  
   Since \( \epsilon \) can be arbitrarily small, this implies:  
   \[
   \mu_n(C) \leq \mu(C).
   \]  

4. **Conclusion**:  
   Taking the supremum over all \( n \), we obtain:  
   \[
   \limsup_n \mu_n(C) \leq \mu(C).
   \]  
   This completes the proof.  

Thus, condition (i) implies condition (ii).  

