- $S = 40$ (number of cars with an in-the-ground swimming pool)
- $N = 35$ (number of cars with neither a two-car guitar nor an in-the-ground swimming pool)

The total number of cars is the sum of cars with a two-car guitar, cars with an in-under-ground swimming pool, cars with both, and cars with neither. 

Using the principle of inclusion-exclusion, the number of cars with either a two-car guitar or an in-under-ground swimming pool is:
\[
\text{Total} = \text{G} + \text{S} - \text{Both} + \text{Neither}
\]
\[
