","To solve this problem, we analyze the system as a system of three masses connected by springs. The stiffness matrix for this system is given by:

\[
K = \begin{bmatrix}
k_t & -K_c & 0 \\
-K_c & k_t & -K_c \\
0 & -K_c & k_t
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Substituting the given values:

\[
K = \begin{bmatrix}
430,000 & -45,430 & 0 \\
-45,430 & 430,000 & -45,430 \\
0 & -45,430 & 430,000
\endbmatrix}
\]

The mass matrix is diagonal and given by:

\[
M = \begin{bmatrix}
m_t & 0 & 0 \\
0 & m_t & 0 \\
0 & 0 & m_t
\end{bmatrix}
\]

Substituting the given value:

\[
M = \begin{bmatrix}
0.0114 & 0 & 0 \\
0 & 0.0114 & 0 \\
0 & 0 & 0.0114
\end{bmatrix}
\]

The natural frequencies are determined by solving the characteristic equation:

\[
\det(K - \omega^2 M) = 0
\]

Expanding the determinant yields:

\[
\det\begin{bmatrix}
430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2 & -45,430 & 0 \\
-45,430 & 430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2 & -45,430 \\
0 & -45,430 & 430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2
\end{bmatrix} = 0
\]

