\[
(430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2)^3 - 2(45,430)^3 = 0
\]

Let \( x = 430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2 \). Then the equation becomes:

\[
x^3 - 2(45,430)^3 = 0
\]

The roots are:

\[
x = 45,430, \quad x = 45,430i, \quad x = -45,430i
\]

Substituting back:

\[
430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2 = 45,430 \implies \omega^2 = \frac{384,570}{0.0114} \implies \omega_1 = 16,600 \, \text{rad/s}
\]

\[
430,000 - 0.0114\omega^2 = -45,430 \implies \omega^2 = \frac{475,430}{0.0114} \implies \omega_2 = 16,700 \, \text{rad}/s
