   \[
   \frac{1 \text{ cm}}{0.1 \text{ cm}} = 10 \text{ strands}.
   \]  
   Thus, there are 10 strands per side of the 1 cm square.  
   The number of 1 cm squares per square meter is:  
   \[
   \frac{1 \text{ m}^2}{(1 \text{ cm})^2} = 10^4 \text{ squares/m}^2.
   \]  
   The total number of strands per square meter is:  
   \[
   10 \text{ strands/side} \times 2 \text{ sides} \times 10^4 \text{ squares/m}^2 = 200,000 \text{ strands/m}^2.
   \]  

2. **Calculate the wetted area per strand**:  
   The wetted area per strand is:  
   \[
   \text{Wetted area} = \text{Stradiance} \times \text{Length} = 1 \text{ m} \times 0.001 \text{ m} = 0.001 \text{ m}^2.
   \]  

3. **Total wetted area**:  
   \[
   \text{Total wetted area} = 200,000 \text{ strands/m}^2 \times 0.001 \text{ m}^2/\text{strand} = 200 \text{ m}^2.
   \]  

