   - Given \( \eta = 0.56 \), solve for \( r \):
     \[
     0.56 = 1 - \frac{1}{r^{1.4 - 1}} \implies 0.56 = 1 - \frac{1}{r^{0.4}}
     \]
     \[
     \frac{1}{r^{0.4}} = 0.44 \implies r^{0.4} = \frac{1}{0.44} \approx 2.273
     \]
     \[
     r = (2.273)^{2.5} \approx 6.5
     \]
