\[ P = \frac{RT}{V} \]  
where \( R \) is the gas constant and \( T \) is the temperature.  

The initial volume is \( V_i \), and the final volume is \( V_f = nV_i \). Substituting \( P \) into the work integral:  
\[ W = \int_{V_i}^{nV_i} \frac{RT}{V} \, dV \]  
\[ W = RT \ln \left( \frac{V_f}{V_i} \right) \]  
\[ W = RT \ln \left( \frac{nV_i}{V_i} \right) \]  
\[ W = RT \ln n \]  

