\[
\Delta E \geq \frac{\hbar}{2\tau},
\]

where \(\hbar\) is the reduced Planck constant (\(1.05 \times 10^{-34} \text{ J s}\)) and \(\tau\) is the lifetime of the particle.

First, convert the lifetime to seconds: \(2.0 \times 10^{-23} \text{ s}\) (this is already in seconds).

